# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights for the React/Vite application following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Package
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` (v1.3.1) to dependencies
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json`

### 2. Modified Files
- **client/src/App.tsx**
  - Imported `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component alongside existing `<Analytics />` component
  - Component is placed at the root level within the `ToastProvider` wrapper for optimal tracking

## Implementation Details

The SpeedInsights component was added following the official guide for React applications (create-react-app/similar frameworks). The component is:
- Imported from `@vercel/speed-insights/react` (the correct React-specific entry point)
- Placed alongside the existing Vercel Analytics component
- Positioned at the application root level to track all routes and page transitions

## Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
